    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1231" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aenēa</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aenīa</span></b> , ae, f., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἴνεια</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of Chalcidice</i>, <i>in Macedonia</i>, <i>opposite Pydna</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 40,
			4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">44, 10</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">32</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aenēātes</span></b> ,
				ĭum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Ænea</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 40, 4,
				4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aenēātĭcus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>belonging to
				Ænea</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">abies,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					16, 39, 76, § 197</span></i>
			.</div>
